{
  "id": "faking",
  "term": "faking",
  "definition": "In psychological assessment, faking is responding on a self-report measure in a way that does not accurately reflect the person, often influenced by social desirability or other biases. It is described as a limitation of questionnaire-based assessment, especially in organizational settings.",
